-# Design Document: 3D Space Splitting Algorithm Implementation
-
-## Overview
-
-The 3D Space Splitting Algorithm (Guillotine Split) is a complete rewrite of the packing engine that replaces the failed step-based approach with a proven 3D Bin Packing Problem (3D-BPP) algorithm. This design addresses critical defects in the original implementation: island gaps in 3D rendering, coordinate axis errors (height incorrectly added to Z-axis), and extremely low space utilization (52%).
-
-### Problem Statement
-
-The original step-based algorithm suffered from fundamental architectural flaws:
-- **Island Gaps**: Artificial spacing based on ETA created visual gaps in 3D rendering
-- **Coordinate Axis Errors**: Height values were accumulated on the Z-axis instead of Y-axis
-- **Low Utilization**: Only 52% space utilization due to inefficient stepping logic
-- **Collision Issues**: currentX += stepping logic caused overlapping cargo
-
-### Solution Approach
-
-This implementation adopts the Guillotine Split algorithm, a standard 3D-BPP technique that:
-- **Maintains Free Space List**: Dynamically tracks available 3D regions within the container
-- **Space Splitting**: After placing cargo, splits the occupied space into three sub-spaces (Top, Right, Front)
-- **Unified Coordinate System**: X=Length (0→12032), Y=Height (0→2698), Z=Width (0→2352)
-- **Zero Artificial Gaps**: Cargo items are placed at exact positions determined by space selection
-- **Target Utilization**: 70-85% space utilization through optimal space selection
-
-### Key Design Principles
-
-1. **Backend Purity**: Backend performs pure 3D-BPP calculation with no rendering concerns
-2. **Frontend Simplicity**: Frontend is "dumb" - renders coordinates without modification
-3. **Center-Aligned Rendering**: mesh.position.set(x + l/2, y + h/2, z + w/2)
-4. **Dual-Dimension Rendering**: Batch outlines (batch.color) + cargo base color (properties.type)
-5. **Physical Constraints**: Heavy cargo (≥20kg) at Y=0, fragile items with no stacking
-
-## Architecture
-
-### System Context
-
-```mermaid
-graph TB
-    subgraph "Frontend (WeChat MiniProgram)"
-        UI[User Interface]
-        TR[ThreeRenderer.js]
-    end
-    
-    subgraph "Backend (Node.js)"
-        API[Packing API]
-        SPE[SimplePackingEngine]
-        CM[Cargo Model]
-        CT[ContainerType Model]
-    end
-    
-    UI -->|Cargo List + Container Type| API
-    API -->|generatePackingPlan| SPE
-    SPE -->|Uses| CM
-    SPE -->|Uses| CT
-    API -->|Packing Result| UI
-    UI -->|Render Data| TR
-    TR -->|3D Visualization| UI
-```
-
-### Algorithm Flow
-
-```mermaid
-flowchart TD
-    Start([Start: Cargo List + Container]) --> Init[Initialize Free Space List]
-    Init --> Expand[Expand Cargo to Single Items]
-    Expand --> Sort[Multi-Dimensional Sort]
-    Sort --> Loop{More Cargo?}
-    
-    Loop -->|Yes| GetCargo[Get Next Cargo Item]
-    GetCargo --> Rotations[Generate Allowed Rotations]
-    Rotations --> TryRot{Try Each Rotation}
-    
-    TryRot --> SelectSpace[Select Best Space]
-    SelectSpace --> CheckSpace{Space Found?}
-    
-    CheckSpace -->|No| NextRot{More Rotations?}
-    NextRot -->|Yes| TryRot
-    NextRot -->|No| Unloaded[Mark as Unloaded]
-    Unloaded --> Loop
-    
-    CheckSpace -->|Yes| CheckHeavy{Heavy Cargo?}
-    CheckHeavy -->|Yes| CheckGround{Space at Y=0?}
-    CheckGround -->|No| NextRot
-    CheckGround -->|Yes| Place[Place Cargo]
-    CheckHeavy -->|No| Place
-    
-    Place --> Split[Split Space into 3 Sub-Spaces]
-    Split --> UpdateList[Update Free Space List]
-    UpdateList --> Loop
-    
-    Loop -->|No| CalcUtil[Calculate Space Utilization]
-    CalcUtil --> CalcDrop[Calculate Drop Order]
-    CalcDrop --> Return([Return Packing Result])
-```
