-# Requirements Document
-
-## Introduction
-
-The 3D Space Splitting Algorithm (Guillotine Split) implementation is a complete rewrite of the packing engine to address critical defects in the original step-based algorithm. The original algorithm suffered from island gaps, coordinate axis errors, and extremely low space utilization (52%). This implementation adopts a standard 3D Bin Packing Problem (3D-BPP) algorithm using space splitting to dynamically maintain free spaces, achieving expected utilization rates of 70-85%.
-
-The system replaces the failed step-based approach with a proven Guillotine Split algorithm that:
-- Eliminates artificial spacing and island gaps in 3D rendering
-- Fixes coordinate axis accumulation errors (Height was incorrectly added to Z-axis)
-- Implements proper space partitioning instead of currentX += stepping logic
-- Maintains a unified coordinate system (X=Length, Y=Height, Z=Width)
-- Enforces physical constraints (heavy cargo, fragile items, inversion rules)
-
-## Glossary
-
-- **Packing_Engine**: The SimplePackingEngine service that implements the 3D space splitting algorithm
-- **Free_Space**: A rectangular 3D region within the container that is available for cargo placement
-- **Space_Splitting**: The process of dividing an occupied space into three sub-spaces (Top, Right, Front) after cargo placement
-- **Guillotine_Split**: A standard 3D-BPP algorithm that cuts spaces using axis-aligned planes
-- **Cargo_Item**: A single physical unit to be packed (expanded from cargo with quantity > 1)
-- **Container**: A shipping container with defined dimensions (innerLength, innerHeight, innerWidth)
-- **Rotation**: A specific orientation of cargo defined by length, height, and width values
-- **Heavy_Cargo**: Cargo with weight >= 20kg that must be placed on the ground (Y=0)
-- **Fragile_Cargo**: Cargo marked as fragile that cannot have items stacked on top
-- **Port_Sequence**: A numeric value indicating loading order based on destination port (higher = load first)
-- **Space_Utilization**: The ratio of packed cargo volume to container volume, expressed as a percentage
-- **Collision**: An overlap between two cargo items in 3D space
-- **AABB**: Axis-Aligned Bounding Box used for collision detection
-- **Coordinate_System**: The unified 3D coordinate system where X=Length, Y=Height, Z=Width
-
-## Requirements
-
-### Requirement 1: Free Space List Initialization
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to initialize the free space list with the entire container volume, so that the algorithm can begin tracking available spaces.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN a packing plan is requested, THE Packing_Engine SHALL create an initial Free_Space representing the entire Container
-2. THE initial Free_Space SHALL have position (x=0, y=0, z=0)
-3. THE initial Free_Space SHALL have dimensions (l=innerLength, h=innerHeight, w=innerWidth)
-4. THE Free_Space list SHALL contain exactly one space before any cargo placement
-
-### Requirement 2: Multi-Dimensional Cargo Sorting
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to sort cargo using multiple criteria, so that optimal packing order is achieved.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Packing_Engine SHALL sort cargo by Port_Sequence in descending order as the first priority
-2. WHEN Port_Sequence values are equal, THE Packing_Engine SHALL sort by weight in descending order
-3. WHEN weight values are equal within 0.01kg tolerance, THE Packing_Engine SHALL sort by volume in descending order
-4. WHEN volume values are equal within 0.01 cubic units tolerance, THE Packing_Engine SHALL sort Fragile_Cargo after non-fragile cargo
-5. THE sorting SHALL be stable (preserve relative order for equal elements)
-
-### Requirement 3: Cargo Expansion to Single Items
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to expand cargo with quantity > 1 into individual items, so that each item can be placed independently.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN cargo has quantity > 1, THE Packing_Engine SHALL create individual Cargo_Item instances for each unit
-2. THE Packing_Engine SHALL preserve all properties (dimensions, weight, constraints) for each expanded Cargo_Item
-3. THE Packing_Engine SHALL assign unique identifiers to each expanded Cargo_Item
-4. WHEN cargo has quantity = 1, THE Packing_Engine SHALL process it as a single Cargo_Item without expansion
-
-### Requirement 4: Optimal Space Selection
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to select the best available space for each cargo item, so that space utilization is maximized.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Packing_Engine SHALL filter Free_Space list to spaces that can fit the Cargo_Item dimensions
-2. WHEN multiple spaces can fit the cargo, THE Packing_Engine SHALL select the space with minimum Y coordinate as first priority
-3. WHEN Y coordinates are equal, THE Packing_Engine SHALL select the space with minimum X coordinate as second priority
-4. WHEN X coordinates are equal, THE Packing_Engine SHALL select the space with minimum Z coordinate as third priority
-5. WHEN all coordinates are equal, THE Packing_Engine SHALL select the space with minimum volume as fourth priority
-6. WHEN no space can fit the cargo, THE Packing_Engine SHALL mark the Cargo_Item as unloaded
-
-### Requirement 5: Space Splitting After Placement
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to split occupied space into three sub-spaces after cargo placement, so that remaining free space is accurately tracked.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN a Cargo_Item is placed in a Free_Space, THE Packing_Engine SHALL remove the original Free_Space from the list
-2. THE Packing_Engine SHALL create a Top_Space above the cargo with position (x=cargo.x, y=cargo.y+cargo.height, z=cargo.z)
-3. THE Top_Space SHALL have dimensions (l=cargo.length, h=original.h-cargo.height, w=cargo.width)
-4. THE Packing_Engine SHALL create a Right_Space to the right of the cargo with position (x=cargo.x, y=cargo.y, z=cargo.z+cargo.width)
-5. THE Right_Space SHALL have dimensions (l=cargo.length, h=original.h, w=original.w-cargo.width)
-6. THE Packing_Engine SHALL create a Front_Space in front of the cargo with position (x=cargo.x+cargo.length, y=cargo.y, z=cargo.z)
-7. THE Front_Space SHALL have dimensions (l=original.l-cargo.length, h=original.h, w=original.w)
-8. THE Packing_Engine SHALL only add sub-spaces with positive dimensions (l>0, h>0, w>0) to the Free_Space list
-
-### Requirement 6: Fragile Cargo Space Splitting
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to prevent stacking on fragile cargo, so that fragile items are not damaged.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN a Fragile_Cargo is placed, THE Packing_Engine SHALL set Top_Space height to 0
-2. THE Packing_Engine SHALL not add the Top_Space to the Free_Space list when height is 0
-3. THE Packing_Engine SHALL create Right_Space and Front_Space normally for Fragile_Cargo
-4. WHEN non-fragile cargo is placed, THE Packing_Engine SHALL create all three sub-spaces with calculated dimensions
-
-### Requirement 7: Heavy Cargo Ground Constraint
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to place heavy cargo on the ground, so that structural stability is maintained.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN cargo weight is >= 20kg, THE Packing_Engine SHALL classify it as Heavy_Cargo
-2. THE Packing_Engine SHALL only place Heavy_Cargo in spaces where y=0
-3. WHEN no ground-level space can fit Heavy_Cargo, THE Packing_Engine SHALL mark it as unloaded
-4. WHEN cargo weight is < 20kg, THE Packing_Engine SHALL allow placement in any suitable Free_Space
-
-### Requirement 8: Rotation Constraint Enforcement
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to respect cargo rotation constraints, so that cargo is not placed in prohibited orientations.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Packing_Engine SHALL always include the original orientation (length, height, width) as an allowed Rotation
-2. WHEN cargo.canInvert is true, THE Packing_Engine SHALL include rotation (length, width, height) as an allowed Rotation
-3. WHEN cargo.canLayFlat is true, THE Packing_Engine SHALL include rotation (height, length, width) as an allowed Rotation
-4. WHEN cargo.canInvert is false, THE Packing_Engine SHALL not allow height-width swapping
-5. WHEN cargo.canLayFlat is false, THE Packing_Engine SHALL not allow height-length swapping
-6. THE Packing_Engine SHALL attempt all allowed rotations when selecting the best space
-
-### Requirement 9: Unified Coordinate System
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to use a unified coordinate system, so that frontend and backend coordinates are consistent.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Packing_Engine SHALL use X-axis to represent Length (0 to innerLength)
-2. THE Packing_Engine SHALL use Y-axis to represent Height (0 to innerHeight)
-3. THE Packing_Engine SHALL use Z-axis to represent Width (0 to innerWidth)
-4. THE Packing_Engine SHALL apply cargo.height to the Y-axis dimension in all calculations
-5. THE Packing_Engine SHALL apply cargo.length to the X-axis dimension in all calculations
-6. THE Packing_Engine SHALL apply cargo.width to the Z-axis dimension in all calculations
-7. THE Packing_Engine SHALL never add height values to Z-axis coordinates
-
-### Requirement 10: Collision Prevention
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to prevent cargo collisions, so that all items fit within their designated spaces.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Packing_Engine SHALL ensure each Cargo_Item is placed entirely within a Free_Space
-2. THE Packing_Engine SHALL verify cargo.x + rotation.length <= space.x + space.l before placement
-3. THE Packing_Engine SHALL verify cargo.y + rotation.height <= space.y + space.h before placement
-4. THE Packing_Engine SHALL verify cargo.z + rotation.width <= space.z + space.w before placement
-5. FOR ALL pairs of loaded cargo items, AABB collision detection SHALL return false (no overlap)
-
-### Requirement 11: Container Boundary Enforcement
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to ensure all cargo stays within container boundaries, so that physical constraints are respected.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Packing_Engine SHALL verify cargo.x + rotation.length <= Container.innerLength for all placed items
-2. THE Packing_Engine SHALL verify cargo.y + rotation.height <= Container.innerHeight for all placed items
-3. THE Packing_Engine SHALL verify cargo.z + rotation.width <= Container.innerWidth for all placed items
-4. THE Packing_Engine SHALL verify cargo.x >= 0, cargo.y >= 0, cargo.z >= 0 for all placed items
-5. WHEN cargo would exceed boundaries, THE Packing_Engine SHALL mark it as unloaded
-
-### Requirement 12: Space Utilization Calculation
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to calculate space utilization accurately, so that packing efficiency can be measured.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Packing_Engine SHALL calculate total cargo volume as the sum of (rotation.length × rotation.height × rotation.width) for all loaded items
-2. THE Packing_Engine SHALL calculate container volume as (innerLength × innerHeight × innerWidth)
-3. THE Packing_Engine SHALL calculate space utilization as (total cargo volume / container volume) × 100
-4. THE Packing_Engine SHALL return space utilization as a percentage value
-5. THE space utilization calculation SHALL use the actual rotation dimensions, not original cargo dimensions
-
-### Requirement 13: Drop Order Calculation
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to calculate drop order for cargo, so that unloading sequence is determined.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Packing_Engine SHALL calculate drop order based on Port_Sequence (higher sequence = earlier drop)
-2. WHEN Port_Sequence values are equal, THE Packing_Engine SHALL use X-coordinate (higher X = earlier drop)
-3. THE Packing_Engine SHALL assign drop order values starting from 1
-4. THE Packing_Engine SHALL ensure cargo with the same Port_Sequence and similar X-coordinates receive the same drop order
-
-### Requirement 14: Packing Result Structure
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to return a structured packing result, so that consumers can access all relevant information.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Packing_Engine SHALL return an object containing loadedCargo array
-2. THE Packing_Engine SHALL return an object containing unloadedCargo array
-3. THE Packing_Engine SHALL return an object containing spaceUtilization percentage
-4. THE Packing_Engine SHALL return an object containing totalWeight value
-5. THE Packing_Engine SHALL return an object containing containerType information
-6. EACH loaded cargo item SHALL include position (x, y, z), rotation (length, height, width), and dropOrder properties
-
-### Requirement 15: Algorithm Performance
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want the algorithm to execute efficiently, so that packing plans are generated quickly.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Packing_Engine SHALL complete packing for 200 cargo items in a 40HQ container within 5 seconds
-2. THE Packing_Engine SHALL complete packing for 500 cargo items in a 40HQ container within 15 seconds
-3. THE Packing_Engine SHALL have time complexity of O(n × m) where n is cargo count and m is average free space count
-4. THE Packing_Engine SHALL limit free space list growth by removing occupied spaces
-
-### Requirement 16: Island Gap Elimination
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to eliminate artificial spacing between cargo, so that 3D rendering shows tightly packed items.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Packing_Engine SHALL not add artificial spacing based on ETA or batch information
-2. THE Packing_Engine SHALL place cargo at the exact position determined by space selection
-3. THE Packing_Engine SHALL not modify X-coordinates to create visual separation between batches
-4. FOR ALL adjacent cargo items, the gap SHALL be 0mm (items touch) or determined by space splitting geometry
-5. THE 3D rendering SHALL show cargo tightly packed without island gaps
-
-### Requirement 17: Parser and Pretty Printer for Packing Plans
-
-**User Story:** As a developer, I want to parse and format packing plans, so that I can serialize and deserialize packing results.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN a valid packing plan JSON is provided, THE Parser SHALL parse it into a PackingPlan object
-2. WHEN an invalid packing plan JSON is provided, THE Parser SHALL return a descriptive error message
-3. THE Pretty_Printer SHALL format PackingPlan objects back into valid JSON strings
-4. FOR ALL valid PackingPlan objects, parsing then printing then parsing SHALL produce an equivalent object (round-trip property)
-5. THE Parser SHALL validate that all required fields (loadedCargo, unloadedCargo, spaceUtilization) are present
-
-### Requirement 18: Space Utilization Target Achievement
-
-**User Story:** As a packing system, I want to achieve 70-85% space utilization, so that container capacity is efficiently used.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN packing typical cargo loads into a 20GP container, THE Packing_Engine SHALL achieve at least 70% space utilization
-2. WHEN packing typical cargo loads into a 40HQ container, THE Packing_Engine SHALL achieve at least 70% space utilization
-3. WHEN packing optimally-sized cargo, THE Packing_Engine SHALL achieve up to 85% space utilization
-4. THE space utilization SHALL be at least 18 percentage points higher than the original step-based algorithm (52%)
-
-### Requirement 19: Backward Compatibility with Frontend
-
-**User Story:** As a frontend developer, I want the packing result format to remain compatible, so that existing 3D rendering code continues to work.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Packing_Engine SHALL return cargo items with position.x, position.y, position.z properties
-2. THE Packing_Engine SHALL return cargo items with rotation.length, rotation.height, rotation.width properties
-3. THE Packing_Engine SHALL return cargo items with all original cargo properties (name, weight, fragile, eta, etc.)
-4. THE Packing_Engine SHALL return cargo items with dropOrder property for unloading sequence
-5. THE returned data structure SHALL be directly consumable by ThreeRenderer.js without transformation
-
-### Requirement 20: Test Coverage for Algorithm Correctness
-
-**User Story:** As a developer, I want comprehensive test coverage, so that algorithm correctness is verified.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE test suite SHALL verify coordinate system correctness (X=Length, Y=Height, Z=Width)
-2. THE test suite SHALL verify multi-dimensional sorting order
-3. THE test suite SHALL verify space splitting logic produces three valid sub-spaces
-4. THE test suite SHALL verify heavy cargo constraint (weight >= 20kg placed at Y=0)
-5. THE test suite SHALL verify fragile cargo constraint (no stacking on fragile items)
-6. THE test suite SHALL verify collision detection using AABB algorithm
-7. THE test suite SHALL verify container boundary enforcement
-8. THE test suite SHALL verify space utilization calculation accuracy
-9. FOR ALL test cases, collision count SHALL equal 0
-10. FOR ALL test cases, all loaded cargo SHALL be within container boundaries
