-# Design Document: v3.2 AI Compliance Timeout Optimization
-
-## Overview
-
-The v3.2 AI Compliance Timeout Optimization feature addresses a critical roadshow issue where AI compliance checks were timing out after 30 seconds, causing "未检测" (not detected) to appear in reports during live demonstrations. This design implements a fast-fail retry mechanism with 5-second timeouts, automatic retry logic, and enhanced physical data fallback to ensure compliance reports are always actionable within 10 seconds.
-
-The architecture follows a "fail fast, fallback gracefully" pattern where AI timeouts trigger immediate retries, and if all attempts fail, the system generates a comprehensive fallback report using physical safety metrics calculated from the packing plan data.
-
-### Design Goals
-
-1. **Fast Failure**: Reduce AI timeout from 30 seconds to 5 seconds per attempt
-2. **Resilience**: Implement automatic retry mechanism for transient failures
-3. **Graceful Degradation**: Provide actionable physical safety metrics when AI is unavailable
-4. **User Experience**: Pre-warm compliance data in background for instant display
-5. **Backward Compatibility**: Maintain v3.1 API interface without frontend changes
-
-### Key Metrics
-
-- **Timeout per attempt**: 5 seconds (reduced from 30 seconds)
-- **Max retry attempts**: 1 (total 2 attempts)
-- **Retry delay**: 500ms
-- **Total max time**: 10 seconds (5s × 2 attempts)
-- **Fallback dimensions**: 6 compliance metrics with physical data
-
