-## Technical Decisions and Rationale
-
-### Decision 1: 5-Second Timeout
-
-**Rationale**: 
-- Original 30-second timeout caused poor user experience during roadshow demos
-- 5 seconds provides reasonable time for AI response while failing fast
-- With 2 attempts, total max time is 10 seconds (acceptable for live demos)
-- DeepSeek-V3 model typically responds in 2-3 seconds, so 5 seconds is sufficient
-
-**Trade-offs**:
-- May increase false negatives if network is slow
-- Mitigated by retry mechanism and fallback reports
-
-### Decision 2: Single Retry (Max 2 Attempts)
-
-**Rationale**:
-- Balances resilience with user experience
-- Two attempts handle transient network issues
-- More retries would exceed 10-second acceptable limit
-- Fallback reports provide value even when AI fails
-
-**Trade-offs**:
-- May not recover from persistent network issues
-- Mitigated by comprehensive physical fallback metrics
-
-### Decision 3: 500ms Retry Delay
-
-**Rationale**:
-- Provides brief pause to allow transient issues to resolve
-- Short enough to keep total time under 10 seconds
-- Prevents immediate retry that might hit same issue
-
-**Trade-offs**:
-- Adds 500ms to total time on retry path
-- Acceptable given 10-second total budget
-
-### Decision 4: Enhanced Physical Fallback
-
-**Rationale**:
-- Provides actionable safety metrics even when AI unavailable
-- Maintains value proposition of compliance check feature
-- Calculates 6 dimensions using physical data from packing plan
-- Shows "AI 超时，无法检测" for dimensions requiring AI analysis
-
-**Trade-offs**:
-- Cannot verify document consistency or hazardous goods without AI
-- Mitigated by clear WARNING indicators and manual review recommendations
-
-### Decision 5: Pre-Warm in onReady
-
-**Rationale**:
-- Fetches compliance data before user interaction
-- Provides instant display when user clicks button
-- Improves perceived performance during demos
-- Silent failure prevents user-facing errors
-
-**Trade-offs**:
-- Uses network bandwidth even if user doesn't click button
-- Acceptable given roadshow demo priority
-
-### Decision 6: Reduced Token Limit (500)
-
-**Rationale**:
-- Reduces AI response time
-- Compliance reports are structured and concise
-- 500 tokens sufficient for 6-dimension report
-
-**Trade-offs**:
-- May truncate very detailed advice
-- Mitigated by structured report format
-
-### Decision 7: Low Temperature (0.1)
-
-**Rationale**:
-- Increases response speed
-- Reduces variability in structured JSON output
-- Compliance checks require deterministic results
-
-**Trade-offs**:
-- Less creative advice text
-- Acceptable for compliance reporting use case
-
-### Decision 8: Maintain v3.1 API Interface
-
-**Rationale**:
-- Zero frontend changes required
-- Reduces deployment risk
-- Maintains backward compatibility
-- Allows gradual rollout
-
-**Trade-offs**:
-- Cannot add new response fields without frontend update
-- Acceptable given emergency optimization priority
-
