-# Requirements Document
-
-## Introduction
-
-The v3.2 AI Compliance Timeout Optimization addresses a critical roadshow issue where AI compliance checks were timing out after 30 seconds, displaying "未检测" (not detected) in reports during live demonstrations. This feature implements a retry mechanism with reduced timeout intervals and enhanced physical data fallback to ensure compliance reports are always actionable within 10 seconds.
-
-## Glossary
-
-- **AI_Compliance_Service**: Backend service that calls AI models to analyze container packing compliance
-- **Physical_Data_Fallback**: Backup compliance report generated from physical measurements when AI times out
-- **Pre_Warm**: Background process that fetches compliance data before user interaction
-- **Retry_Mechanism**: Logic that attempts failed AI calls multiple times with shorter timeouts
-- **VGM**: Verified Gross Mass - container weight verification requirement
-- **CoG**: Center of Gravity - weight distribution measurement
-
-## Requirements
-
-### Requirement 1: Reduce AI Timeout Duration
-
-**User Story:** As a roadshow presenter, I want AI compliance checks to fail fast, so that I don't wait 30 seconds for timeout errors during live demos.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN an AI compliance check is initiated, THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL set the timeout to 5 seconds per attempt
-2. THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL replace the 30-second timeout with a 5-second timeout
-3. WHEN the 5-second timeout expires, THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL proceed to retry logic without blocking
-
-### Requirement 2: Implement Retry Mechanism
-
-**User Story:** As a system operator, I want automatic retries for failed AI calls, so that transient network issues don't cause false negatives.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN an AI compliance check times out, THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL retry the request once
-2. THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL wait 500 milliseconds between retry attempts
-3. THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL limit total attempts to 2 (1 initial + 1 retry)
-4. WHEN both attempts fail, THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL invoke physical data fallback within 10 seconds total
-
-### Requirement 3: Enhanced Physical Data Fallback
-
-**User Story:** As a compliance officer, I want to see physical safety metrics even when AI times out, so that I can still assess basic container safety.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN AI compliance check fails, THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL generate a fallback report with physical metrics
-2. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL accept a summary parameter containing packing plan data
-3. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL calculate VGM status and display "未提交 VGM" with WARNING level when VGM is not submitted
-4. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL calculate load capacity from totalWeight plus tare weight and display PASS or FAIL status
-5. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL calculate CoG offset from lateral and longitudinal offset values and display PASS or FAIL status
-6. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL display "AI 超时，无法检测" with WARNING level for document consistency checks
-7. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL display "AI 超时，无法检测" with WARNING level for hazardous goods compliance
-8. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL evaluate cargo mixing compatibility from mixingProhibition data and display PASS or FAIL status
-9. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL include physical metrics in the advice field when available
-
-### Requirement 4: Pre-Warm Compliance Data
-
-**User Story:** As a roadshow presenter, I want compliance data loaded in the background, so that reports appear instantly when I click the button.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN a packing plan is generated, THE Pre_Warm SHALL silently fetch compliance report in the background
-2. THE Pre_Warm SHALL be invoked in the onReady lifecycle hook of packing-result page
-3. THE Pre_Warm SHALL not block user interface rendering
-4. WHEN the user clicks the compliance button, THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL return cached results if available
-5. THE Pre_Warm SHALL handle failures silently without displaying errors to users
-
-### Requirement 5: Physical Metrics Display Format
-
-**User Story:** As a compliance officer, I want physical metrics displayed in a structured table, so that I can quickly scan safety dimensions.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL generate a report table with 6 compliance dimensions
-2. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL format VGM dimension with status and description
-3. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL format load capacity dimension with calculated weight ratio and limit comparison
-4. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL format CoG dimension with lateral and longitudinal offset values
-5. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL format document consistency dimension with timeout indicator
-6. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL format hazardous goods dimension with timeout indicator
-7. THE Physical_Data_Fallback SHALL format cargo mixing dimension with prohibition rule evaluation
-
-### Requirement 6: Timeout Error Handling
-
-**User Story:** As a system administrator, I want timeout errors logged with context, so that I can diagnose AI service issues.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN an AI timeout occurs, THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL log the timeout event with timestamp
-2. WHEN retry logic is triggered, THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL log the retry attempt number
-3. WHEN fallback is activated, THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL log the reason for fallback activation
-4. THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL include request payload size in timeout logs
-5. IF both attempts fail, THEN THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL log the total elapsed time
-
-### Requirement 7: Backward Compatibility
-
-**User Story:** As a developer, I want the optimized service to work with existing code, so that no frontend changes are required.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL maintain the same API interface as v3.1
-2. THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL return the same response structure for successful AI calls
-3. THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL return fallback reports in the same format as AI reports
-4. WHEN called from existing frontend code, THE AI_Compliance_Service SHALL function without modifications
-5. THE Pre_Warm SHALL integrate with existing packing-result.js without breaking changes
