-# Design Document: AI Compliance UX View-Recheck Separation
-
-## Overview
-
-This design document specifies the technical implementation for separating "view historical report" and "trigger new check" functionality in the AI compliance feature. The solution introduces a visual indicator (document icon) for cached reports while ensuring the main button always triggers a new compliance check with user confirmation.
-
-### Design Goals
-
-1. **Clear Visual Separation**: Users can distinguish between viewing cached data and triggering new analysis
-2. **State-Controlled Behavior**: Implement a simple state machine to manage UI transitions
-3. **Memory-Enabled Architecture**: Persist compliance reports during the session for quick reference
-4. **Professional UX**: Provide loading states, error handling, and smooth transitions
-5. **Canvas Overlay Compatibility**: Ensure all UI elements display correctly above the WebGL 3D canvas
-
-### Key Technical Challenges
-
-- **Canvas Z-Index Management**: WeChat Mini Program `<canvas type="webgl">` has special rendering behavior that requires `<cover-view>` for overlays
-- **State Synchronization**: Maintain consistency between `complianceReport` data and UI visibility states
-- **Touch Target Optimization**: Ensure document icon and main button have separate, accurate hit areas
-- **API Call Prevention**: Implement loading states to prevent duplicate requests during processing
-
-## Architecture
-
-### Component Structure
-
-```
-Packing Result Page
-├── AI Compliance Button (Main Trigger)
-│   ├── Document Icon (cover-view, conditional)
-│   └── Button Text + Loading State
-├── Compliance Report Popup (cover-view modal)
-│   ├── Header (Title + Close Button)
-│   ├── Status Card (Score + Badge)
-│   ├── Issues List (Scrollable)
-│   ├── Advice Section (Scrollable)
-│   ├── Timestamp Footer
-│   └── Refresh Button (New Re-check Trigger)
-└── Re-check Confirmation Dialog (wx.showModal)
-```
-
-
-### State Machine Design
-
-The feature implements a simple three-state machine:
-
-```
-State: IDLE
-├── complianceReport: null
-├── showComplianceReport: false
-├── isCheckingCompliance: false
-└── Document Icon: Hidden
-
-State: LOADING
-├── complianceReport: null or previous value
-├── showComplianceReport: false
-├── isCheckingCompliance: true
-└── Document Icon: Hidden or Visible (based on previous report)
-
-State: SHOWING_REPORT
-├── complianceReport: { status, score, issues, advice, timestamp }
-├── showComplianceReport: true
-├── isCheckingCompliance: false
-└── Document Icon: Visible (when popup closed)
-```
-
-### State Transitions
-
-```
-IDLE --[onAIComplianceCheck + confirm]--> LOADING
-LOADING --[API success]--> SHOWING_REPORT
-LOADING --[API failure]--> IDLE (with error toast)
-SHOWING_REPORT --[onCloseComplianceReport]--> IDLE (with cached report)
-SHOWING_REPORT --[onRefreshReport + confirm]--> LOADING
-IDLE (with cached report) --[onViewReport]--> SHOWING_REPORT
-```
-
-## Components and Interfaces
-
-### 1. Document Icon (View History Indicator)
-
-**Purpose**: Visual indicator that a cached compliance report exists
-
-**Implementation**:
-- Element Type: `<cover-view>` (required for canvas overlay)
-- Position: Absolute positioning in top-right corner of AI_Compliance_Button
-- Visibility: Conditional rendering based on `complianceReport !== null`
-- Touch Target: 44rpx × 44rpx minimum (accessibility requirement)
-
-**WXML Structure**:
-```xml
-<view class="ai-compliance-section">
-  <button class="ai-compliance-btn" bindtap="onAIComplianceCheck">
-    🤖 AI 港口合规体检
-  </button>
-  
-  <!-- Document Icon - Only visible when report exists -->
-  <cover-view 
