-## Correctness Properties
-
-*A property is a characteristic or behavior that should hold true across all valid executions of a system-essentially, a formal statement about what the system should do. Properties serve as the bridge between human-readable specifications and machine-verifiable correctness guarantees.*
-
-### Property Reflection Analysis
-
-After analyzing all acceptance criteria, the following redundancies were identified:
-
-**Redundant Properties Eliminated:**
-- 1.2 is redundant with 1.1 (inverse of same conditional rendering)
-- 3.3 is redundant with 3.2 (no API call is part of direct display behavior)
-- 6.1 is redundant with 2.6 (same state update requirement)
-- 6.4 is redundant with 1.1 (same visibility condition)
-- 7.3 is redundant with 7.2 and 1.1 (icon visibility follows from unchanged report state)
-- 7.6 is redundant with 3.5 (same error message requirement)
-
-**Properties Combined:**
-- 2.6 and 2.7 can be combined into a single property about API success handling
-- 4.4 and 4.5 can be combined into a single property about refresh flow
-
-### Property 1: Document Icon Conditional Rendering
-
-*For any* page state, the Document Icon SHALL be visible if and only if `complianceReport` is not null
-
-**Validates: Requirements 1.1, 1.2, 6.4**
-
-### Property 2: Document Icon Click Handler
-
-*For any* click event on the Document Icon, the system SHALL invoke the `onViewReport` method without calling the API
-
-**Validates: Requirements 1.5**
-
-### Property 3: Main Button Click Handler
-
-*For any* click event on the AI_Compliance_Button, the system SHALL invoke the `onAIComplianceCheck` method and display the confirmation dialog
-
-**Validates: Requirements 1.6, 2.1**
-
-### Property 4: Confirmation Dialog Always Shows
-
-*For any* state of `complianceReport` (null or populated), calling `onAIComplianceCheck` SHALL display the confirmation dialog
-
-**Validates: Requirements 2.5**
-
-
-### Property 5: Confirmation Triggers API Call
-
-*For any* confirmation dialog acceptance, the system SHALL call the AI compliance API endpoint
-
-**Validates: Requirements 2.3**
-
-### Property 6: Cancellation Prevents API Call
-
-*For any* confirmation dialog cancellation, the system SHALL NOT call the AI compliance API
-
-**Validates: Requirements 2.4**
-
-### Property 7: API Success Updates State and Shows Popup
-
-*For any* successful API response, the system SHALL update `complianceReport` with the new data AND set `showComplianceReport` to true
-
-**Validates: Requirements 2.6, 2.7**
-
-### Property 8: View Report Direct Display
-
-*For any* invocation of `onViewReport` with non-null `complianceReport`, the system SHALL set `showComplianceReport` to true without calling the API
-
-**Validates: Requirements 3.2, 3.3**
-
-### Property 9: View Report No Confirmation Dialog
-
-*For any* invocation of `onViewReport`, the system SHALL NOT display the confirmation dialog
-
-**Validates: Requirements 3.4**
-
-### Property 10: Refresh Button Triggers Confirmation
-
-*For any* click event on the Refresh Button, the system SHALL display the confirmation dialog
-
-**Validates: Requirements 4.3**
-
-### Property 11: Refresh Flow Updates Report
-
-*For any* refresh confirmation acceptance, the system SHALL call the API and update the Report_Popup content with new results while keeping `showComplianceReport` true
-
-**Validates: Requirements 4.4, 4.5, 4.6**
-
-### Property 12: Loading State During API Call
-
-*For any* active API call, the system SHALL set `isCheckingCompliance` to true and display loading indicators on both the main button and refresh button
-
-**Validates: Requirements 4.7, 7.4**
-
-### Property 13: Button Disabled During API Call
-
-*For any* active API call, the AI_Compliance_Button SHALL be disabled to prevent duplicate requests
-
-**Validates: Requirements 7.5**
-
-### Property 14: State Persistence Across Operations
-
-*For any* `complianceReport` value, it SHALL persist in memory until either a new check completes or the page is unloaded
-
-**Validates: Requirements 6.2**
-
-### Property 15: Memory Cleanup on Page Unload
-
-*For any* page unload event, the system SHALL clear the `complianceReport` from memory
-
-**Validates: Requirements 6.5**
-
-### Property 16: API Failure Error Handling
-
-*For any* failed API response, the system SHALL display an error message and NOT update `complianceReport`
-
-**Validates: Requirements 7.1, 7.2, 7.3**
-
