-# Requirements Document
-
-## Introduction
-
-This feature optimizes the AI compliance check UX by separating "view historical report" and "trigger new check" functionality. Currently, the system directly shows a cached report popup when clicking the AI compliance button if a report exists, making it unclear whether users are viewing historical data or triggering a new check. This creates confusion during roadshow demonstrations where clarity is essential.
-
-The solution introduces a dedicated visual indicator (document icon) for viewing cached reports while ensuring the main button always triggers a new compliance check. This transforms the system into a state-controlled, memory-enabled professional logistics platform.
-
-## Glossary
-
-- **AI_Compliance_Button**: The main "AI 港口合规体检" button in the packing result page
-- **Document_Icon**: A floating cover-view icon displayed in the top-right corner of the AI_Compliance_Button
-- **Cached_Report**: The stored compliance report data in `complianceReport` variable
-- **Report_Popup**: The 92-point scoring popup modal that displays compliance check results
-- **Re-check_Dialog**: The confirmation dialog asking "是否重新体检" before triggering a new API call
-- **Refresh_Button**: A prominent button in the Report_Popup's top-right corner for triggering re-checks while viewing reports
-- **Packing_Result_Page**: The miniprogram page at `miniprogram/pages/packing-result/`
-
-## Requirements
-
-### Requirement 1: Visual Separation of View and Re-check Actions
-
-**User Story:** As a logistics operator, I want to clearly distinguish between viewing historical reports and triggering new compliance checks, so that I understand whether I'm looking at cached data or initiating a fresh analysis.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN `complianceReport` is not empty, THE Document_Icon SHALL be visible in the top-right corner of the AI_Compliance_Button
-2. WHEN `complianceReport` is empty, THE Document_Icon SHALL NOT be displayed
-3. THE Document_Icon SHALL use a document/file visual representation to indicate "view history"
-4. THE Document_Icon SHALL be implemented as a `cover-view` element for proper layering
-5. WHEN a user clicks the Document_Icon, THE System SHALL invoke the `onViewReport` method
-6. WHEN a user clicks the AI_Compliance_Button main area, THE System SHALL invoke the `onAIComplianceCheck` method
-
-### Requirement 2: Re-check Functionality Always Triggers New Analysis
-
-**User Story:** As a roadshow presenter, I want the main compliance button to always trigger a new check with confirmation, so that I can demonstrate the system's real-time analysis capabilities clearly.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN a user clicks the AI_Compliance_Button, THE System SHALL display the Re-check_Dialog
-2. THE Re-check_Dialog SHALL contain the text "是否重新体检"
-3. WHEN a user confirms the Re-check_Dialog, THE System SHALL call the AI compliance API
-4. WHEN a user cancels the Re-check_Dialog, THE System SHALL NOT call the API and SHALL close the dialog
-5. THE `onAIComplianceCheck` method SHALL NOT check for existing `complianceReport` before showing the dialog
-6. WHEN the API call completes successfully, THE System SHALL update `complianceReport` with the new data
-7. WHEN the API call completes successfully, THE System SHALL display the Report_Popup with the new results
-
-### Requirement 3: Dedicated View Historical Report Method
-
-**User Story:** As a logistics operator, I want to quickly view my last compliance report without triggering a new check, so that I can reference previous results efficiently.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE System SHALL implement a new `onViewReport` method in `packing-result.js`
-2. WHEN `onViewReport` is invoked, THE System SHALL directly display the Report_Popup with `complianceReport` data
-3. THE `onViewReport` method SHALL NOT call the AI compliance API
-4. THE `onViewReport` method SHALL NOT display the Re-check_Dialog
-5. WHEN `complianceReport` is empty and `onViewReport` is invoked, THE System SHALL display an error message "暂无历史报告"
-
-### Requirement 4: In-Report Re-check Capability
-
-**User Story:** As a logistics operator, I want to trigger a new compliance check while viewing a historical report, so that I can compare results or update my analysis without closing the popup.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Report_Popup SHALL display a Refresh_Button in its top-right corner
-2. THE Refresh_Button SHALL use a refresh/reload icon visual representation
-3. WHEN a user clicks the Refresh_Button, THE System SHALL display the Re-check_Dialog
-4. WHEN a user confirms the re-check from within the Report_Popup, THE System SHALL call the AI compliance API
-5. WHEN the API call completes successfully, THE System SHALL update the Report_Popup content with new results
-6. THE Report_Popup SHALL remain open during the re-check process
-7. WHILE the API call is in progress, THE Refresh_Button SHALL display a loading indicator
-
-### Requirement 5: Visual Styling and Layout Consistency
-
-**User Story:** As a user, I want the new UI elements to match the existing design language, so that the interface feels cohesive and professional.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Document_Icon SHALL be positioned in the top-right corner with 8rpx padding from edges
-2. THE Document_Icon SHALL have a size of 40rpx × 40rpx
-3. THE Document_Icon SHALL use a semi-transparent white background with 0.9 opacity
-4. THE Document_Icon SHALL have a border-radius of 50% for circular appearance
-5. THE Refresh_Button SHALL match the existing button styling in the Report_Popup
-6. THE Refresh_Button SHALL be positioned in the top-right corner of the Report_Popup header
-7. THE existing 92-point report popup style SHALL remain unchanged except for the Refresh_Button addition
-
-### Requirement 6: State Management and Memory Behavior
-
-**User Story:** As a system administrator, I want the compliance report cache to persist during the session, so that users can reference historical data without unnecessary API calls.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN a new compliance check completes, THE System SHALL store the result in `complianceReport`
-2. THE `complianceReport` SHALL persist until the page is unloaded or a new check is performed
-3. WHEN the Packing_Result_Page is loaded, THE System SHALL check for existing `complianceReport` data
-4. WHEN `complianceReport` exists on page load, THE Document_Icon SHALL be visible immediately
-5. WHEN a user navigates away and returns to the Packing_Result_Page, THE `complianceReport` SHALL be cleared (session-based memory)
-
-### Requirement 7: Error Handling and User Feedback
-
-**User Story:** As a logistics operator, I want clear feedback when operations fail, so that I understand what went wrong and can take appropriate action.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN the AI compliance API call fails, THE System SHALL display an error message with the failure reason
-2. WHEN the API call fails, THE System SHALL NOT update `complianceReport`
-3. WHEN the API call fails, THE Document_Icon visibility SHALL remain unchanged
-4. WHILE an API call is in progress, THE AI_Compliance_Button SHALL display a loading indicator
-5. WHILE an API call is in progress, THE AI_Compliance_Button SHALL be disabled to prevent duplicate requests
-6. WHEN a user attempts to view a report but `complianceReport` is empty, THE System SHALL display "暂无历史报告"
-
-### Requirement 8: Accessibility and Touch Target Optimization
-
-**User Story:** As a mobile user, I want touch targets to be appropriately sized and positioned, so that I can accurately tap the intended controls.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Document_Icon SHALL have a minimum touch target size of 44rpx × 44rpx
-2. THE Document_Icon SHALL NOT overlap with the AI_Compliance_Button text
-3. THE Refresh_Button SHALL have a minimum touch target size of 44rpx × 44rpx
-4. WHEN a user taps near the Document_Icon boundary, THE System SHALL register the tap on the Document_Icon
-5. THE AI_Compliance_Button main area SHALL remain tappable without accidentally triggering the Document_Icon
