-# Design Document: Layered Packing 70% Optimization
-
-## Overview
-
-This design specifies optimizations to the LayeredPackingEngine to achieve ≥70% space utilization for the Cixi appliances test case (200 air fryers + 100 heaters + 80 fans in a 40HQ container). The current implementation achieves 44.09% utilization with 100% loading rate.
-
-The optimization strategy focuses on four key areas:
-1. **Adaptive Grid Size**: Reduce discretization waste by calculating optimal grid size based on cargo dimensions
-2. **Dynamic Layer Heights**: Eliminate vertical space waste by calculating layer heights based on actual stacked items
-3. **Space-Optimized Rotations**: Maximize floor space efficiency by prioritizing footprint area minimization
-4. **Intelligent Layer Assignment**: Improve packing density by optimizing item-to-layer allocation
-
-All optimizations use simple rule-based logic without complex algorithms, maintain the forced layering approach, and complete within 10 seconds.
-
-### Current State Analysis
-
-The existing LayeredPackingEngine has these characteristics:
-- Fixed 100mm grid size causes discretization waste (items snap to 100mm boundaries)
-- Fixed layer heights (1400mm, 1200mm, 98mm) waste vertical space
-- Rotation selection prioritizes height minimization over footprint area
-- Layer assignment uses fixed rules without considering remaining space optimization
-
-### Target Improvements
-
-To achieve 70% utilization from 44.09%, we need to recover approximately 25.91 percentage points of wasted space:
-- **Grid optimization**: Recover ~5-8% by reducing grid size from 100mm to 50mm or less
-- **Layer height optimization**: Recover ~10-15% by eliminating vertical gaps
-- **Rotation optimization**: Recover ~5-8% by improving floor space usage
-- **Layer assignment optimization**: Recover ~3-5% by better item grouping
-
-## Architecture
-
-The optimization maintains the existing LayeredPackingEngine architecture with enhancements to four core methods:
-
-```
-LayeredPackingEngine
-├── generatePackingPlan() [ENHANCED]
-│   ├── _calculateOptimalGridSize() [NEW]
-│   ├── _classifyCargoByType()
-│   ├── _createDynamicLayers() [NEW - replaces fixed layerRules]
-│   └── _loadLayer() [ENHANCED]
-│       ├── _fillLayerWithGrid() [ENHANCED]
-│       │   ├── _getBestRotationForSpace() [NEW - replaces _getBestRotation]
-│       │   └── _findAvailablePosition() [ENHANCED]
-│       └── _optimizeLayerHeight() [NEW]
-├── _calculateSpaceUtilization()
-├── _calculateTotalWeight()
-├── _calculateCenterOfGravity()
-├── _calculateLoadDistribution()
-├── _simpleComplianceCheck()
-└── _generateVisualizationData()
-```
-
-### Key Architectural Decisions
-
-1. **Maintain Layered Approach**: Keep the forced layering strategy as it provides predictable, debuggable behavior
-2. **Incremental Optimization**: Apply optimizations sequentially so each can be tested independently
-3. **Backward Compatibility**: Preserve existing method signatures and return structures
-4. **Fallback Strategy**: If optimization fails to achieve 70%, log warning and return best attempt
-
-## Components and Interfaces
-
-### 1. Adaptive Grid Size Calculator
-
-**Purpose**: Calculate optimal grid size based on cargo dimensions to minimize discretization waste.
-
-**Algorithm**:
-```javascript
-_calculateOptimalGridSize(cargoList) {
-  // Step 1: Extract all unique dimensions from cargo
-  const dimensions = new Set();
-  cargoList.forEach(cargo => {
-    dimensions.add(cargo.length);
-    dimensions.add(cargo.width);
-    dimensions.add(cargo.height);
-  });
-  
-  // Step 2: Calculate GCD of all dimensions
-  const dimArray = Array.from(dimensions);
-  let gcd = dimArray[0];
-  for (let i = 1; i < dimArray.length; i++) {
-    gcd = this._gcd(gcd, dimArray[i]);
-  }
-  
-  // Step 3: Apply constraints (10mm min, 50mm max)
-  if (gcd < 10) gcd = 10;
-  if (gcd > 50) gcd = 50;
-  
-  return gcd;
-}
-
-_gcd(a, b) {
-  return b === 0 ? a : this._gcd(b, a % b);
-}
-```
-
-**Input**: Array of cargo objects with dimensions (length, width, height)
-**Output**: Integer grid size in mm (10-50mm range)
-**Constraints**: 
-- Must handle edge cases (single dimension, all same dimensions)
-- Must complete in <100ms for up to 500 items
-
-### 2. Dynamic Layer Height Allocator
-
-**Purpose**: Calculate layer heights dynamically based on actual stacked items to eliminate vertical waste.
-
-**Algorithm**:
-```javascript
-_createDynamicLayers(cargoByType, containerType) {
-  const layers = [];
-  let currentZ = 0;
-  
-  // Step 1: Analyze cargo stacking potential
-  const stackableGroups = this._analyzeStackingGroups(cargoByType);
-  
-  // Step 2: Create layers based on stacking groups
-  for (const group of stackableGroups) {
-    const layerHeight = this._calculateRequiredHeight(group);
-    
-    // Ensure layer fits in remaining space
-    if (currentZ + layerHeight > containerType.innerHeight) {
-      break;
-    }
-    
-    layers.push({
-      name: `Layer_${layers.length + 1}`,
-      cargoTypes: group.types,
-      zStart: currentZ,
-      maxHeight: layerHeight,
-      priority: layers.length + 1
-    });
-    
-    currentZ += layerHeight;
-  }
-  
-  // Step 3: Allocate remaining vertical space
-  if (currentZ < containerType.innerHeight) {
-    const remainingHeight = containerType.innerHeight - currentZ;
-    // Distribute to layers proportionally or create final layer
-    this._allocateRemainingSpace(layers, remainingHeight);
-  }
-  
-  return layers;
-}
-
-_analyzeStackingGroups(cargoByType) {
-  // Group 1: Stackable items with high stack limits (air fryers, heaters)
-  // Group 2: Non-stackable items (fans)
-  // Group 3: Remaining stackable items
-  
-  const groups = [];
-  
-  // Prioritize stackable items for bottom layers
-  const stackable = Object.entries(cargoByType)
-    .filter(([name, items]) => items[0]?.cargo?.stackable)
-    .sort((a, b) => {
-      // Sort by stack limit descending
-      return (b[1][0]?.cargo?.maxStackLayers || 1) - 
-             (a[1][0]?.cargo?.maxStackLayers || 1);
-    });
-  
-  if (stackable.length > 0) {
-    groups.push({
-      types: stackable.map(([name]) => name),
-      stackable: true,
-      maxStackLayers: Math.max(...stackable.map(([, items]) => 
-        items[0]?.cargo?.maxStackLayers || 1))
-    });
-  }
-  
-  // Non-stackable items in middle
-  const nonStackable = Object.entries(cargoByType)
-    .filter(([name, items]) => !items[0]?.cargo?.stackable)
-    .map(([name]) => name);
-  
-  if (nonStackable.length > 0) {
-    groups.push({
-      types: nonStackable,
-      stackable: false,
-      maxStackLayers: 1
-    });
-  }
-  
-  return groups;
-}
-
-_calculateRequiredHeight(group) {
-  // Calculate height needed for this group
-  // For stackable: item_height × max_stack_layers
-  // For non-stackable: item_height
-  // Add 50mm clearance for safety
-  
-  let maxHeight = 0;
-  
-  group.types.forEach(typeName => {
-    const items = cargoByType[typeName];
-    if (items && items.length > 0) {
-      const item = items[0].cargo;
-      const stackHeight = item.height * (group.maxStackLayers || 1);
-      maxHeight = Math.max(maxHeight, stackHeight);
-    }
-  });
-  
-  return maxHeight + 50; // Add clearance
-}
-```
-
-**Input**: Classified cargo by type, container dimensions
-**Output**: Array of layer definitions with dynamic heights
-**Constraints**:
-- Total layer heights must not exceed container height
-- Each layer must accommodate at least one item
-- Vertical waste per layer must be <100mm
-
-### 3. Space-Optimized Rotation Selector
-
-**Purpose**: Select item rotations that minimize footprint area to maximize floor space usage.
-
-**Algorithm**:
-```javascript
-_getBestRotationForSpace(cargo, maxHeight, containerType) {
-  // Generate all 6 possible rotations
-  const rotations = [
-    { length: cargo.length, width: cargo.width, height: cargo.height, id: 'LWH' },
-    { length: cargo.width, width: cargo.length, height: cargo.height, id: 'WLH' },
-    { length: cargo.length, width: cargo.height, height: cargo.width, id: 'LHW' },
-    { length: cargo.height, width: cargo.width, height: cargo.length, id: 'HWL' },
-    { length: cargo.width, width: cargo.height, height: cargo.length, id: 'WHL' },
-    { length: cargo.height, width: cargo.length, height: cargo.width, id: 'HLW' }
-  ];
-  
-  // Step 1: Filter by height constraint
-  let validRotations = rotations.filter(r => r.height <= maxHeight);
-  
-  // Step 2: Filter by container dimensions
-  validRotations = validRotations.filter(r => 
-    r.length <= containerType.innerLength && 
-    r.width <= containerType.innerWidth
-  );
-  
-  if (validRotations.length === 0) {
-    return null;
-  }
-  
-  // Step 3: Calculate footprint area for each rotation
-  validRotations.forEach(r => {
-    r.footprintArea = r.length * r.width;
-  });
-  
-  // Step 4: Sort by footprint area (ascending) then height (ascending)
-  validRotations.sort((a, b) => {
-    const areaDiff = a.footprintArea - b.footprintArea;
-    // If areas within 5%, prefer shorter height
-    if (Math.abs(areaDiff) / a.footprintArea < 0.05) {
-      return a.height - b.height;
-    }
-    return areaDiff;
-  });
-  
-  return validRotations[0];
-}
-```
-
-**Input**: Cargo object, maximum layer height, container dimensions
-**Output**: Optimal rotation object with length, width, height
-**Constraints**:
-- Must evaluate all 6 orientations
-- Must respect container dimension limits
-- Must prioritize footprint area over height
-
-### 4. Intelligent Layer Assignment Strategy
-
-**Purpose**: Optimize item-to-layer allocation to maximize packing density.
-
-**Algorithm**:
-```javascript
-_fillLayerWithGrid(layer, cargoItems, plan, containerType, startOrder) {
-  let loadingOrder = startOrder;
-  
-  // Step 1: Sort items by footprint area (descending)
-  // Place larger items first to avoid fragmentation
-  const sortedItems = [...cargoItems].sort((a, b) => {
-    const areaA = a.length * a.width;
-    const areaB = b.length * b.width;
-    return areaB - areaA;
-  });
-  
-  // Step 2: Track layer utilization
-  const layerState = {
-    usedArea: 0,
-    totalArea: containerType.innerLength * containerType.innerWidth,
-    placedItems: 0
-  };
-  
-  for (const cargo of sortedItems) {
-    // Select best rotation for space optimization
-    const rotation = this._getBestRotationForSpace(
-      cargo, 
-      layer.maxHeight, 
-      containerType
-    );
-    
-    if (!rotation) {
-      plan.unloadedCargo.push({
-        cargo: cargo,
-        reason: `No valid rotation for ${layer.name}`
-      });
-      continue;
-    }
-    
-    // Find position using adaptive grid
