-# Requirements Document
-
-## Introduction
-
-This document specifies requirements for optimizing the LayeredPackingEngine to achieve ≥70% space utilization for the Cixi appliances test case (200 air fryers + 100 heaters + 80 fans in a 40HQ container). The current implementation achieves 44.09% utilization with 100% loading rate. The optimization must use simple manual rules without complex algorithms, maintain the forced layering approach, and complete computation within 10 seconds.
-
-## Glossary
-
-- **LayeredPackingEngine**: The packing algorithm that divides container vertical space into horizontal layers and places items within each layer
-- **Space_Utilization**: Percentage of container volume occupied by cargo, calculated as (total cargo volume / container volume) × 100
-- **Loading_Rate**: Percentage of requested items successfully loaded into the container
-- **Grid_Size**: The discretization unit (currently 100mm) used for positioning items on the container floor
-- **Layer_Height**: The vertical height allocated to each horizontal packing layer
-- **Rotation_Strategy**: The logic that selects which orientation (length×width×height permutation) to use for each item
-- **40HQ_Container**: A 40-foot high-cube shipping container with dimensions 12032×2352×2698mm and 26680kg max weight
-- **Stackable_Item**: An item that can have other items placed on top of it, with a maximum stack limit
-- **Non_Stackable_Item**: An item that cannot have other items placed on top of it
-- **Cixi_Test_Case**: The specific cargo mix of 200 air fryers (300×300×350mm, 5kg, stackable×4) + 100 heaters (500×400×600mm, 8kg, stackable×3) + 80 fans (400×400×1200mm, 6kg, non-stackable)
-
-## Requirements
-
-### Requirement 1: Adaptive Grid Size
-
-**User Story:** As a logistics planner, I want the packing engine to use an appropriate grid size for the cargo dimensions, so that space is not wasted due to excessive discretization.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN cargo items are provided, THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL calculate a grid size based on the greatest common divisor (GCD) of all cargo dimensions
-2. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL use a grid size no larger than 50mm for the Cixi test case
-3. WHEN the calculated grid size is less than 10mm, THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL use 10mm as the minimum grid size
-4. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL align all item placements to the calculated grid size
-5. FOR ALL valid cargo sets, reducing grid size from 100mm to 50mm or less SHALL NOT decrease the loading rate below 100%
-
-### Requirement 2: Optimized Layer Height Allocation
-
-**User Story:** As a logistics planner, I want the packing engine to allocate layer heights efficiently, so that vertical space is fully utilized without leaving unusable gaps.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN creating layers, THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL calculate layer heights based on the actual stacked heights of items assigned to each layer
-2. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL NOT leave more than 100mm of unused vertical space in any layer
-3. WHEN stackable items are placed, THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL calculate the layer height as (item_height × stack_count) plus any required clearance
-4. WHEN non-stackable items are placed, THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL calculate the layer height as the item height plus any required clearance
-5. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL allocate remaining vertical space to layers in proportion to their space utilization potential
-
-### Requirement 3: Space-Optimized Rotation Selection
-
-**User Story:** As a logistics planner, I want the packing engine to select item rotations that maximize space utilization, so that more items fit in each layer.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN selecting a rotation for an item, THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL evaluate all 6 possible orientations (length×width×height permutations)
-2. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL prioritize rotations that minimize the footprint area (length × width) over rotations that minimize height
-3. WHEN multiple rotations have similar footprint areas (within 5% difference), THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL select the rotation with the smallest height
-4. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL reject rotations where any dimension exceeds the corresponding container dimension
-5. FOR ALL items in the Cixi test case, the selected rotation SHALL result in a footprint area no larger than the current implementation's rotation selection
-
-### Requirement 4: Improved Layer Assignment Strategy
-
-**User Story:** As a logistics planner, I want the packing engine to assign items to layers intelligently, so that each layer's capacity is fully utilized.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN assigning items to layers, THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL prioritize filling lower layers before creating new upper layers
-2. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL assign stackable items with higher stack limits to lower layers
-3. WHEN a layer has remaining space, THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL attempt to fit smaller items before closing the layer
-4. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL group items with similar heights in the same layer to minimize wasted vertical space
-5. WHEN non-stackable items are assigned, THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL place them in dedicated layers or as top items in mixed layers
-
-### Requirement 5: 70% Space Utilization Target
-
-**User Story:** As a logistics planner, I want the packing engine to achieve at least 70% space utilization for the Cixi test case, so that the roadshow demo demonstrates significant improvement.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN packing the Cixi test case (200 air fryers + 100 heaters + 80 fans), THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL achieve space utilization ≥70%
-2. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL maintain 100% loading rate for all three item types in the Cixi test case
-3. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL complete the packing computation within 10 seconds
-4. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL respect all weight constraints (total weight ≤26680kg for 40HQ container)
-5. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL respect all stacking constraints (air fryers ≤4 layers, heaters ≤3 layers, fans non-stackable)
-
-### Requirement 6: 3D Visualization Data Generation
-
-**User Story:** As a roadshow presenter, I want the packing engine to generate complete 3D visualization data, so that I can demonstrate the optimized packing layout to customers.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN packing is complete, THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL generate position data (x, y, z coordinates) for every placed item
-2. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL generate dimension data (length, width, height) for every placed item in its placed orientation
-3. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL generate layer boundary data showing the height ranges of each layer
-4. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL generate summary statistics including space utilization percentage, loading rate percentage, and total weight
-5. THE Visualization_Data SHALL be formatted as JSON compatible with the existing 3D rendering system
-
-### Requirement 7: Backward Compatibility
-
-**User Story:** As a developer, I want the optimized packing engine to maintain compatibility with existing interfaces, so that integration with the rest of the system requires minimal changes.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL accept the same input format as the current implementation (cargo array with dimensions, weight, quantity, stackLimit)
-2. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL return the same output structure as the current implementation (placedItems array, summary object, visualization data)
-3. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL be invokable through the existing test script (backend/scripts/test-layered-packing.js) without modifications
-4. WHEN the optimization fails to achieve 70% utilization, THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL fall back to the current implementation and log a warning
-5. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL maintain the existing API contract for integration with the backend routes
-
-### Requirement 8: Performance and Simplicity
-
-**User Story:** As a developer, I want the packing engine to use simple rule-based optimizations, so that the code remains maintainable and debuggable for the roadshow timeline.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL NOT use complex algorithms such as Guillotine, Maximal Rectangles, or AI-based approaches
-2. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL complete packing computation within 10 seconds for cargo sets up to 500 items
-3. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL use deterministic rules that produce consistent results for the same input
-4. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL log intermediate steps (layer creation, item placement, rotation selection) for debugging purposes
-5. THE LayeredPackingEngine SHALL include inline comments explaining the optimization logic for future maintenance
