-# Requirements Document
-
-## Introduction
-
-This document specifies the requirements for the Port Dynamics Dashboard feature, which displays real-time port updates and route information for Ningbo Port on the miniprogram homepage. The dashboard provides users with timely notifications about port entry dynamics, route changes, and operational updates through a visually prominent card interface with automatic content rotation.
-
-## Glossary
-
-- **Dashboard**: The Port Dynamics Dashboard card component displaying real-time port updates
-- **Miniprogram**: The WeChat miniprogram application
-- **Homepage**: The main index page of the miniprogram (pages/index/index)
-- **四宫格**: The 4-grid core function area on the homepage
-- **Vertical_Swiper**: A WeChat swiper component configured for vertical scrolling with autoplay
-- **Update_Type**: Classification of port updates (urgent, warning, info, normal)
-- **Port_API**: The backend API endpoint `/api/port/updates`
-- **Fallback_Data**: Static port update data used when the API is unavailable
-
-## Requirements
-
-### Requirement 1: Dashboard Layout Integration
-
-**User Story:** As a miniprogram user, I want to see the port dynamics dashboard prominently on the homepage, so that I can quickly access real-time port information.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Dashboard SHALL be positioned immediately after the 四宫格 component in the homepage WXML layout
-2. THE Dashboard SHALL display a header with the text "宁波港实时航线与入港动态" and a 📢 icon
-3. THE Dashboard SHALL have a card width of 90% with margin set to 40rpx auto to align with the 四宫格 width
-4. THE Dashboard SHALL use a Vertical_Swiper component to display port updates
-
-### Requirement 2: Real-time Data Integration
-
-**User Story:** As a miniprogram user, I want to receive real-time port updates from the backend API, so that I have access to the latest port information.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN the Homepage loads, THE Miniprogram SHALL send a GET request to the Port_API endpoint
-2. WHEN the Port_API responds successfully, THE Dashboard SHALL display the returned port updates
-3. THE Port_API SHALL return an array of update objects containing type, title, content, and timestamp fields
-4. WHEN a port update is received, THE Dashboard SHALL display the update within 500ms
-
-### Requirement 3: Disaster Recovery Fallback
-
-**User Story:** As a miniprogram user, I want to see port information even when the API is unavailable, so that I always have access to some port data.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. IF the Port_API request fails, THEN THE Miniprogram SHALL use Fallback_Data
-2. IF the Port_API request exceeds 5000ms timeout, THEN THE Miniprogram SHALL use Fallback_Data
-3. THE Fallback_Data SHALL contain at least 3 sample port updates with valid type, title, content, and timestamp fields
-4. WHEN Fallback_Data is used, THE Dashboard SHALL display the fallback updates without error messages
-
-### Requirement 4: Automatic Content Rotation
-
-**User Story:** As a miniprogram user, I want port updates to rotate automatically, so that I can see multiple updates without manual interaction.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Vertical_Swiper SHALL automatically advance to the next update every 3000ms
-2. THE Vertical_Swiper SHALL display one update at a time in vertical orientation
-3. WHEN the last update is displayed, THE Vertical_Swiper SHALL loop back to the first update
-4. THE Vertical_Swiper SHALL have a height sufficient to display one complete update card
-
-### Requirement 5: Visual Design and Styling
-
-**User Story:** As a miniprogram user, I want the dashboard to be visually appealing and easy to read, so that I can quickly understand port updates.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Dashboard SHALL use a card design with box-shadow for depth effect
-2. THE Dashboard SHALL apply a gradient background to the card
-3. WHEN Update_Type is "urgent", THE Dashboard SHALL display a red label
-4. WHEN Update_Type is "warning", THE Dashboard SHALL display an orange label
-5. WHEN Update_Type is "info", THE Dashboard SHALL display a blue label
-6. WHEN Update_Type is "normal", THE Dashboard SHALL display a green label
-7. THE Dashboard SHALL display update title, content, and timestamp in a readable font hierarchy
-
-### Requirement 6: Backend API Implementation
-
-**User Story:** As a backend system, I want to provide a port updates endpoint, so that the miniprogram can fetch real-time port data.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Port_API SHALL respond to GET requests at `/api/port/updates`
-2. THE Port_API SHALL return a JSON array of port update objects
-3. THE Port_API SHALL include type, title, content, and timestamp fields in each update object
-4. THE Port_API SHALL respond within 3000ms under normal conditions
-5. THE Port_API SHALL return HTTP 200 status code for successful requests
-6. IF no updates are available, THEN THE Port_API SHALL return an empty array with HTTP 200 status
-
-### Requirement 7: Data Validation
-
-**User Story:** As a miniprogram developer, I want to ensure data integrity, so that the dashboard displays valid information.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN port update data is received, THE Miniprogram SHALL validate that each update contains required fields (type, title, content, timestamp)
-2. IF an update is missing required fields, THEN THE Miniprogram SHALL exclude that update from display
-3. THE Miniprogram SHALL validate that Update_Type is one of: "urgent", "warning", "info", or "normal"
-4. IF Update_Type is invalid, THEN THE Miniprogram SHALL default to "normal" type styling
-
-### Requirement 8: Performance Requirements
-
-**User Story:** As a miniprogram user, I want the dashboard to load quickly, so that it doesn't slow down the homepage.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Dashboard SHALL render within 1000ms of homepage load
-2. THE Port_API request SHALL not block rendering of other homepage components
-3. THE Vertical_Swiper animation SHALL maintain 30fps or higher during transitions
-4. THE Dashboard SHALL consume less than 5MB of memory during normal operation
