-## Fix Implementation
-
-### Changes Required
-
-Assuming our root cause analysis is correct, we will implement three surgical fixes:
-
-**File**: `backend/services/Realistic4DPackingEngine.js`
-
-### Change 1: Coordinate Inversion in buildResult() (Lines ~444-509)
-
-**Current Code Pattern:**
-```javascript
-buildResult(expandedCargo) {
-  const packedItems = this.placements.map(p => ({
-    x: p.x,  // ❌ Direct assignment - first packed at X=0 (door)
-    y: p.y,
-    z: p.z,
-    // ...
-  }));
-}
-```
-
-**Fixed Code (Invert Result Method):**
-```javascript
-buildResult(expandedCargo) {
-  const packedItems = this.placements.map(p => ({
-    x: this.container.innerLength - (p.x + p.length),  // ✅ Invert X coordinate
-    y: p.y,  // Y unchanged (ground to ceiling)
-    z: p.z,  // Z unchanged (left to right)
-    length: p.length,
-    width: p.width,
-    height: p.height,
-    // ... rest unchanged
-  }));
-}
-```
-
-**Rationale**: 
-- Keep algorithm packing 0→L normally (no collision math changes)
-- Invert coordinates in post-processing to place Port 3 (first packed) at far end (wall)
-- Place Port 1 (last packed) at near end (door)
-- Safer than reversing iteration logic in `generateCandidates()`
-
-### Change 2: Classification Logic Fix in mapPackagingTypeToFrontend() (Lines ~415-442 and ~510-537)
-
-**Current Code Pattern:**
-```javascript
-mapPackagingTypeToFrontend(packagingType, weight, fragile) {
-  if (fragile === true) {
-    return 'fragile';
-  }
-  if (weight >= 20) {
-    return 'heavy';
-  }
-  // ❌ Missing else clause - returns undefined for normal cargo
-}
-```
-
-**Fixed Code (Strict 3-Tier Hierarchy):**
-```javascript
-mapPackagingTypeToFrontend(packagingType, weight, fragile) {
-  // 1. Highest Priority: Physical property
-  if (fragile === true) {
-    return 'fragile';
-  }
-  
-  // 2. Second Priority: Weight Threshold (20kg)
-  if (weight >= 20) {
-    return 'heavy';
-  }
-  
-  // 3. Default Fallback (CRITICAL FIX: Missing 'else')
-  return 'normal';  // ✅ Explicit default for all other cargo
-}
-```
-
-**Rationale**:
-- Fragile is highest priority (physical property overrides weight)
-- Heavy is second priority (weight threshold)
-- Normal is default fallback (ensures all cargo gets classified)
-- Fixes undefined returns for standard cargo
-
-**Note**: This function appears twice in the file (lines ~415 and ~510) - both instances must be fixed identically.
-
-### Change 3: Multi-Level Sort Enhancement in sortCargo() (Lines ~140-151)
-
-**Current Code Pattern:**
-```javascript
-sortCargo(cargoList) {
-  return cargoList.sort((a, b) => {
-    // Only sorts by portSequence
-    if (a.portSequence !== b.portSequence) {
-      return b.portSequence - a.portSequence; // DESC: 3, 2, 1
-    }
-    return 0;  // ❌ No secondary sorting criteria
-  });
-}
-```
-
-**Fixed Code (Multi-Level Sort):**
-```javascript
-sortCargo(cargoList) {
-  return cargoList.sort((a, b) => {
-    // 1. Strict Batch Separation (High Port = Deep in container)
-    if (a.portSequence !== b.portSequence) {
-      return b.portSequence - a.portSequence; // DESC: 3, 2, 1
-    }
-    
-    // 2. Heavy items at bottom (if stacked within same batch)
-    if (a.weight >= 20 && b.weight < 20) return -1;
-    if (a.weight < 20 && b.weight >= 20) return 1;
-    
-    // 3. Volume DESC (Standard packing heuristic - larger items first)
-    return (b.length * b.width * b.height) - (a.length * a.width * a.height);
-  });
-}
-```
-
-**Rationale**:
-- Level 1: Batch separation (portSequence DESC) - ensures LIFO compliance
-- Level 2: Heavy items first within batch - improves stability
-- Level 3: Volume DESC - standard bin packing heuristic for better utilization
-- Combined with coordinate inversion, ensures proper spatial batch zones
-
