-# Bugfix Requirements Document
-
-## Introduction
-
-This document addresses three critical P0 production issues blocking the roadshow demonstration:
-
-1. **Model Configuration Failure**: Backend fails to apply DeepSeek-V3 configuration despite .env file changes
-2. **UI Blocking & Scroll Issues**: WeChat cover-view causing content overflow and inaccessibility
-3. **VGM Business Logic Error**: AI incorrectly treating VGM as a calculated parameter instead of validating user input
-
-These issues prevent proper AI model operation, block user access to critical content, and cause false compliance errors that undermine system credibility.
-
-## Bug Analysis
-
-### Current Behavior (Defect)
-
-#### Issue 1: Model Configuration Failure
-
-1.1 WHEN backend starts after .env file is modified to use DeepSeek-V3 THEN the system continues running Qwen model without loading new configuration
-
-1.2 WHEN environment variables are changed in .env file THEN the system does not reload configuration without explicit dotenv override flag
-
-1.3 WHEN backend console logs startup information THEN the system does not display "API Model Configured: DeepSeek-V3" confirmation
-
-#### Issue 2: UI Blocking & Scroll Issues
-
-1.4 WHEN packing result page renders with cover-view containing internal content THEN the system causes content overflow that is not scrollable
-
-1.5 WHEN content exceeds cover-view height restrictions THEN the system truncates text and makes it inaccessible to users
-
-1.6 WHEN cover-view attempts to use overflow-y: scroll THEN the system fails because WeChat cover-view does not support this CSS property
-
-#### Issue 3: VGM Business Logic Error
-
-1.7 WHEN AI compliance check processes VGM (Verified Gross Mass) THEN the system incorrectly attempts to calculate/infer VGM value
-
-1.8 WHEN user has not yet filled in VGM declaration weight THEN the system shows "not submitted" error warnings incorrectly
-
-1.9 WHEN AI processes compliance data THEN the system treats VGM as an AI-calculated parameter causing FAIL status inappropriately
-
-### Expected Behavior (Correct)
-
-#### Issue 1: Model Configuration Failure
-
-2.1 WHEN backend starts with modified .env file THEN the system SHALL forcefully reload environment variables using dotenv with override: true flag
-
-2.2 WHEN backend initializes AI configuration THEN the system SHALL log "API Model Configured: DeepSeek-V3" to console for verification
-
-2.3 WHEN configuration changes are applied THEN the system SHALL require killing all node.exe processes (Windows) and restarting to ensure clean state
-
-#### Issue 2: UI Blocking & Scroll Issues
-
-2.4 WHEN packing result page renders content THEN the system SHALL remove outer cover-view height restrictions to allow content expansion
-
-2.5 WHEN content needs to be scrollable THEN the system SHALL replace cover-view with scroll-view or WeChat native page-container component
-
-2.6 WHEN advice-box displays content THEN the system SHALL set explicit height or allow auto-expansion based on content without truncation
-
-2.7 WHEN scroll-view is nested in cover-view THEN the system SHALL verify WeChat version compatibility or use alternative approach
-
-#### Issue 3: VGM Business Logic Error
-
-2.8 WHEN AI compliance check processes VGM THEN the system SHALL stop AI from inferring or calculating VGM values
-
-2.9 WHEN packing plan page loads THEN the system SHALL display "VGM Declaration Weight" input field for user entry
-
-2.10 WHEN user enters VGM declaration weight THEN the system SHALL implement local validation logic: VGM_error = |actual_total_weight - declared_VGM| / declared_VGM
-
-2.11 WHEN backend calculates VGM error and result > 5% THEN the system SHALL set reportTable dimension status to FAIL
-
-2.12 WHEN AI summarizes compliance results THEN the system SHALL only summarize physical results without calculating VGM
-
-2.13 WHEN user has not filled in VGM data THEN the system SHALL only show error if validation is triggered by user action
-
-### Unchanged Behavior (Regression Prevention)
-
-#### Issue 1: Model Configuration Failure
-
-3.1 WHEN backend uses other environment variables (database, ports, etc.) THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO load them correctly
-
-3.2 WHEN AI model processes requests after configuration THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO maintain existing API interface contracts
-
-#### Issue 2: UI Blocking & Scroll Issues
-
-3.3 WHEN packing result page displays 3D visualization THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO render correctly
-
-3.4 WHEN user interacts with other UI elements on packing result page THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO function normally
-
-3.5 WHEN page layout uses other WeChat components THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO display properly
-
-#### Issue 3: VGM Business Logic Error
-
-3.6 WHEN AI compliance check validates other parameters (weight distribution, stacking rules, etc.) THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO perform AI-based validation
-
-3.7 WHEN compliance report displays non-VGM dimensions THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO show AI-calculated results
-
-3.8 WHEN user views compliance summary THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO display overall compliance status correctly
-
-3.9 WHEN backend calculates actual_total_weight from packing results THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO compute accurately
