-# Design Document: SKU-Level 3D Worker Interface
-
-## Overview
-
-This design document specifies the technical implementation for transforming the existing 3D packing visualization into an operational blueprint for warehouse workers. The feature adds three critical worker-facing interactions: SKU filtering with ghost transparency mode, click-to-inspect functionality, and a cargo details panel.
-
-### Design Goals
-
-1. **Zero Backend Changes**: All functionality implemented in frontend only
-2. **Performance First**: Maintain 30+ FPS with 500+ cargo items
-3. **WeChat Compatibility**: Handle touch events and canvas limitations
-4. **Material Efficiency**: Minimize material object creation and updates
-5. **Worker Productivity**: Sub-100ms response time for all interactions
-
-### Key Technical Challenges
-
-1. **Material Management**: Updating opacity on hundreds of meshes without lag
-2. **Touch Event Mapping**: Converting WeChat touch coordinates to Three.js NDC
-3. **Memory Efficiency**: Avoiding material cloning for each mesh
-4. **Raycaster Performance**: Real-time intersection detection without frame drops
-
-## Architecture
-
-### Component Hierarchy
-
-```
-packing-result.js (Page Controller)
-├── Data Layer
-│   ├── rawPackingData (Non-reactive cargo array)
-│   ├── uniqueSkuList (Extracted from loadedCargo)
-│   └── selectedSkus (User filter selections)
-├── UI Layer
-│   ├── SKU_Filter_Panel (WXML checkboxes)
-│   ├── Cargo_Inspector (Toast/Modal)
-│   └── 3D Canvas (WebGL)
-└── ThreeRenderer.js (3D Engine)
-    ├── Material Manager
-    ├── Raycaster System
-    └── Visibility Controller
-```
-
-### Data Flow Diagram
-
-```
-Backend API Response
-    ↓
-packing-result.js receives loadedCargo[]
-    ↓
-Extract unique SKU names → uniqueSkuList
-    ↓
-Render SKU_Filter_Panel (WXML)
-    ↓
-User selects SKUs → selectedSkus[]
-    ↓
-ThreeRenderer.updateSkuVisibility(selectedSkus)
-    ↓
-For each mesh in cargoGroup:
-    - If mesh.userData.name in selectedSkus → opacity = 1.0
-    - Else → opacity = 0.15
-    ↓
-Render scene (needsRender = true)
-
-Touch Event on Canvas
-    ↓
-packing-result.js onCanvasTap(e)
-    ↓
-Extract touch.x, touch.y
-    ↓
-ThreeRenderer.detectCargoClick(x, y, canvasWidth, canvasHeight)
-    ↓
-Raycaster.setFromCamera(mouse, camera)
-    ↓
-Raycaster.intersectObjects(cargoGroup.children)
-    ↓
-Return mesh.userData or null
-    ↓
-packing-result.js displays Cargo_Inspector
-```
-
-## Components and Interfaces
-
-### 1. SKU Filter Panel (packing-result.js)
-
-#### Data Extraction Method
-
-```javascript
-/**
- * Extract unique SKU names from loaded cargo
- * @param {Array} loadedCargo - Backend API response cargo array
- * @returns {Array} uniqueSkuList - Array of unique product names
- */
-generateUniqueSkuList(loadedCargo) {
-  const skuSet = new Set();
-  
-  loadedCargo.forEach(item => {
-    // Primary: use 'name' field
-    const skuName = item.name || item.sku || 'Unknown';
-    skuSet.add(skuName);
-  });
-  
-  return Array.from(skuSet).sort();
-}
-```
