-# Requirements Document
-
-## Introduction
-
-This feature transforms the existing 3D packing visualization into an operational blueprint for warehouse workers. Currently, the Realistic4DPackingEngine produces optimal LIFO interleaved loading plans, but workers can only see colored batches without knowing specific product details. This upgrade enables workers to identify exact cargo items (washing machines, air fryers, etc.) at each coordinate, allowing them to load containers with 100% fidelity to the algorithm's space utilization plan.
-
-This is a frontend-only enhancement that adds three critical worker-facing interactions: SKU filtering with ghost transparency mode, click-to-inspect functionality, and a cargo details panel. No backend algorithm changes are required.
-
-## Glossary
-
-- **SKU_Filter_Panel**: UI component displaying unique product names extracted from packing results
-- **Ghost_Transparency_Mode**: Visual rendering state where unselected cargo appears semi-transparent (opacity 0.15) while selected cargo remains opaque
-- **Raycaster**: Three.js mechanism for detecting 3D object intersections with mouse/touch input
-- **Cargo_Inspector**: UI component displaying detailed product information when a box is clicked
-- **ThreeRenderer**: Frontend 3D rendering engine using three-platformize for WeChat Mini Program
-- **Packing_Result_Page**: Frontend page displaying 3D visualization of packed containers
-- **Backend_API**: Server endpoint returning packing data with cargo details
-- **Mesh_UserData**: Three.js mesh property storing cargo metadata (name, sku, dimensions, weight, batch)
-
-## Requirements
-
-### Requirement 1: Parse Backend Packing Data
-
-**User Story:** As a warehouse worker, I want the system to extract all unique product names from the packing results, so that I can see what types of cargo are in the container.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN the Packing_Result_Page receives backend packing data, THE SKU_Filter_Panel SHALL extract all unique product names from the cargo array
-2. THE SKU_Filter_Panel SHALL use the `name` field as the primary identifier for each unique product
-3. IF the `name` field is not present, THEN THE SKU_Filter_Panel SHALL use the `sku` field as fallback
-4. THE SKU_Filter_Panel SHALL remove duplicate product names before rendering
-5. THE SKU_Filter_Panel SHALL preserve the original product name strings without modification
-
-### Requirement 2: Render SKU Filter Panel
-
-**User Story:** As a warehouse worker, I want to see a list of all cargo types in the container, so that I can select which products to highlight in the 3D view.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE SKU_Filter_Panel SHALL render all unique product names as selectable UI elements
-2. THE SKU_Filter_Panel SHALL display product names in a visually accessible format (checkboxes or toggle buttons)
-3. THE SKU_Filter_Panel SHALL allow multiple product selections simultaneously
-4. THE SKU_Filter_Panel SHALL provide a "Select All" option to show all cargo types
-5. THE SKU_Filter_Panel SHALL provide a "Clear All" option to reset selections
-
-### Requirement 3: Implement Ghost Transparency Mode
-
-**User Story:** As a warehouse worker, I want to see through layers of unselected cargo while keeping my target products visible, so that I can locate exactly where specific items should be placed in the container.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN a worker selects one or more products in the SKU_Filter_Panel, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL apply Ghost_Transparency_Mode to all cargo meshes
-2. FOR ALL selected products, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL set mesh material opacity to 1.0 (fully opaque)
-3. FOR ALL unselected products, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL set mesh material opacity to 0.15 (semi-transparent)
-4. FOR ALL cargo meshes, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL set material transparent property to true
-5. FOR ALL selected products, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL set mesh material depthWrite to true
-6. FOR ALL unselected products, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL set mesh material depthWrite to false
-7. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL preserve spatial reference by keeping all cargo meshes visible (visible property remains true)
-8. WHEN no products are selected, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL render all cargo meshes at full opacity (opacity 1.0)
-
-### Requirement 4: Store Cargo Metadata in Mesh UserData
-
-**User Story:** As a system developer, I want each 3D mesh to contain complete cargo information, so that workers can inspect product details by clicking on boxes.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN the ThreeRenderer creates a cargo mesh, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL store cargo metadata in mesh.userData
-2. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL store the product name in mesh.userData.name
-3. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL store the SKU identifier in mesh.userData.sku
-4. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL store cargo dimensions in mesh.userData (length, width, height)
-5. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL store cargo weight in mesh.userData.weight
-6. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL store batch identifier in mesh.userData.batch
-7. FOR ALL cargo meshes, THE mesh.userData SHALL contain all fields required by the Cargo_Inspector
-
-### Requirement 5: Implement 3D Touch Click Interaction
-
-**User Story:** As a warehouse worker, I want to tap any box in the 3D view and immediately see what product it represents, so that I can verify I'm loading the correct item.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL initialize a Raycaster for detecting mesh intersections
-2. WHEN a worker clicks or touches the 3D canvas, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL cast a ray from the touch point into the 3D scene
-3. THE Raycaster SHALL detect intersections with all visible cargo meshes
-4. WHEN the Raycaster detects an intersection, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL extract mesh.userData from the intersected mesh
-5. WHEN no intersection is detected, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL take no action
-6. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL handle both mouse click events (desktop) and touch events (mobile)
-
-### Requirement 6: Display Cargo Inspector Panel
-
-**User Story:** As a warehouse worker, I want to see detailed product information when I tap a box, so that I can confirm dimensions, weight, and batch before loading.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN a cargo mesh is clicked, THE Cargo_Inspector SHALL display product information extracted from mesh.userData
-2. THE Cargo_Inspector SHALL display the product name in the format "Product Name: {name}"
-3. THE Cargo_Inspector SHALL display dimensions in the format "Dimensions: {L}x{W}x{H}"
-4. THE Cargo_Inspector SHALL display weight in the format "Weight: {weight}kg"
-5. THE Cargo_Inspector SHALL display batch in the format "Batch: {batch}"
-6. THE Cargo_Inspector SHALL position the information panel at the top of the interface or as a toast notification
-7. THE Cargo_Inspector SHALL remain visible until the worker clicks another box or dismisses the panel
-8. THE Cargo_Inspector SHALL handle missing userData fields gracefully by displaying "N/A" for unavailable information
-
-### Requirement 7: Verify Backend API Data Structure
-
-**User Story:** As a system developer, I want to confirm the backend API returns all required cargo fields, so that the frontend can display complete product information.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE Backend_API SHALL return cargo data containing a `name` or `sku` field for each item
-2. THE Backend_API SHALL return cargo dimensions (length, width, height) for each item
-3. THE Backend_API SHALL return cargo weight for each item
-4. THE Backend_API SHALL return batch identifier for each item
-5. IF any required field is missing, THEN THE Packing_Result_Page SHALL log a warning and use fallback values
-
-### Requirement 8: Integrate with Existing ThreeRenderer
-
-**User Story:** As a system developer, I want to extend the existing ThreeRenderer without breaking current functionality, so that batch color visualization and camera controls continue to work.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL preserve existing batch color rendering functionality
-2. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL preserve existing camera controls (rotate, zoom, pan)
-3. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL preserve existing container boundary visualization
-4. WHEN Ghost_Transparency_Mode is active, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL maintain batch color differentiation for selected cargo
-5. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL update the rendering loop to handle transparency sorting correctly
-
-### Requirement 9: Performance Optimization for Worker Interface
-
-**User Story:** As a warehouse worker, I want the 3D interface to respond instantly when I filter or click cargo, so that I can work efficiently without waiting for rendering updates.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. WHEN a worker changes SKU filter selections, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL update mesh opacity within 100 milliseconds
-2. WHEN a worker clicks a cargo mesh, THE Cargo_Inspector SHALL display information within 50 milliseconds
-3. THE Raycaster SHALL perform intersection tests on every frame without causing frame rate drops below 30 FPS
-4. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL batch material property updates to minimize rendering overhead
-5. FOR ALL transparency updates, THE ThreeRenderer SHALL avoid recreating mesh geometries or materials
-
-### Requirement 10: WeChat Mini Program Compatibility
-
-**User Story:** As a system developer, I want all new features to work seamlessly in the WeChat Mini Program environment, so that workers can use the interface on mobile devices.
-
-#### Acceptance Criteria
-
-1. THE ThreeRenderer SHALL use three-platformize for all Three.js operations
-2. THE SKU_Filter_Panel SHALL use WeChat Mini Program native components (checkbox, button)
-3. THE Cargo_Inspector SHALL use WeChat Mini Program native UI elements (view, text)
-4. THE Raycaster SHALL handle WeChat Mini Program touch events correctly
-5. THE Packing_Result_Page SHALL test all interactions on WeChat Developer Tools before deployment
-
-## Technical Context
-
-- **Frontend Framework**: WeChat Mini Program
-- **3D Rendering Library**: Three.js via three-platformize
-- **Key Files**: 
-  - `miniprogram/pages/packing-result/packing-result.js`
-  - `miniprogram/utils/ThreeRenderer.js`
-- **Backend**: Realistic4DPackingEngine (no changes required)
-- **Data Flow**: Backend API → Packing Result Page → ThreeRenderer → Worker Interface
-
-## Success Criteria
-
-This feature will be considered successful when:
-1. Workers can filter cargo by product name and see ghost transparency mode working correctly
-2. Workers can tap any box and immediately see product details (name, dimensions, weight, batch)
-3. The interface responds within 100ms for all interactions
-4. All existing 3D visualization features (batch colors, camera controls) continue to work
-5. The feature works reliably in WeChat Mini Program on mobile devices
