-## Introduction
-
-The v23.0.0 Fluid Solid Packing algorithm (DBLFPackingEngine) fails to load ANY items from Batch 3 (0 out of 187 items) when processing a 3-batch scenario with LIFO constraints. This occurs because Batch 3 has the earliest unload time (portSeq=1, ETA 2024-01-05) and therefore cannot rest on Batch 1 or Batch 2 cargo. By the time the algorithm attempts to place Batch 3 items, the container ground space is already occupied by later-unloading batches, creating a deadlock where Batch 3 cannot satisfy both the 85% support requirement and the LIFO constraint simultaneously.
-
-**Impact**: Critical - Complete failure to load an entire batch, resulting in 83.29% utilization (below 85% target) and potential business disruption for time-sensitive cargo.
-
-**Test Case**: 587 items in 3 batches (200+200+187) in 20GP container (5898×2393×2352mm)
-- Batch 1: portSeq=3, ETA 2024-01-15, 200/200 loaded ✅
-- Batch 2: portSeq=2, ETA 2024-01-10, 184/200 loaded ⚠️
-- Batch 3: portSeq=1, ETA 2024-01-05, 0/187 loaded ❌
-
-## Bug Analysis
-
-### Current Behavior (Defect)
-
-1.1 WHEN Batch 3 (earliest unload, portSeq=1) is processed after Batch 1 and Batch 2 have occupied ground space THEN the system fails to place ANY Batch 3 items (0/187 loaded)
-
-1.2 WHEN the algorithm attempts to place Batch 3 cargo at Y>0 positions THEN the system rejects all placements because they would rest on later-unloading batches (violating LIFO constraint)
-
-1.3 WHEN the algorithm attempts to place Batch 3 cargo at Y=0 positions THEN the system finds no available ground space because Batch 1 and Batch 2 have already occupied it
-
-1.4 WHEN the conflicting requirements (85% support + LIFO constraint) create a deadlock THEN the system produces no error message or warning, silently failing to load the entire batch
-
-1.5 WHEN Batch 3 fails to load THEN the system reports 83.29% utilization, below the 85% target, without indicating the root cause
-
-### Expected Behavior (Correct)
-
-2.1 WHEN Batch 3 (earliest unload, portSeq=1) is processed THEN the system SHALL successfully load at least 150+ items (80%+ of 187 items) while respecting LIFO constraints
-
-2.2 WHEN the algorithm encounters LIFO-constrained placements THEN the system SHALL apply progressive support relaxation (85% → 80% → 75% → 70%) to find valid placement points
-
-2.3 WHEN multiple batches have different unload times THEN the system SHALL pack batches in reverse portSequence order (earliest unload first) to prioritize ground space for LIFO-constrained batches
-
-2.4 WHEN a batch cannot find placement due to conflicting constraints THEN the system SHALL provide clear diagnostic messages indicating the constraint conflict and attempted relaxation strategies
-
-2.5 WHEN all batches are successfully placed THEN the system SHALL achieve 85%+ overall utilization while maintaining all physical constraints (support, LIFO, stability)
-
-### Unchanged Behavior (Regression Prevention)
-
-3.1 WHEN processing single-batch scenarios (no LIFO constraints) THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO achieve 85%+ utilization with 85% support requirement
-
-3.2 WHEN processing batches with identical portSequence values THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO pack them in input order without LIFO restrictions
-
-3.3 WHEN placing cargo at Y=0 (ground level) THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO require no support validation
-
-3.4 WHEN calculating support percentage for cargo at Y>0 THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO use the formula: (supported bottom area / total bottom area) × 100%
-
-3.5 WHEN validating LIFO constraints THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO prevent cargo from resting on later-unloading batches (higher portSequence values)
-
-3.6 WHEN generating 3D visualization data THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO provide accurate position, rotation, and batch information for all placed cargo
-
-3.7 WHEN processing Batch 1 and Batch 2 in the current test case THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO load 200/200 and 184/200 items respectively with existing placement logic
