-# Bugfix Requirements Document
-
-## Introduction
-
-The v32.0 Realistic4DPackingEngine produces physically impossible results: 131.09% space utilization and gray-colored cargo boxes in 3D visualization. This emergency fix addresses critical defects in collision detection, data structure consistency, and visual rendering that make the system unusable for production demonstrations.
-
-**Impact**: CRITICAL - User has zero tolerance for >100% utilization. System credibility is at stake.
-
-**Scope**: This bugfix targets the v33.0 engine integration across backend API response formatting, frontend color rendering, and error handling for impossible utilization values.
-
-## Bug Analysis
-
-### Current Behavior (Defect)
-
-1.1 WHEN the packing engine calculates space utilization THEN the system reports 131.09% utilization (physically impossible)
-
-1.2 WHEN cargo is placed in the container THEN the system allows cargo to overlap freely without collision detection
-
-1.3 WHEN the backend sends packing results to the frontend THEN the system uses nested `properties` object structure that the frontend cannot parse
-
-1.4 WHEN the frontend renders cargo boxes in 3D THEN the system displays gray boxes instead of vibrant colors
-
-1.5 WHEN the frontend reads color data from cargo objects THEN the system looks for `cargo.renderColor` field which doesn't exist in v33.0 response
-
-1.6 WHEN the 3D renderer applies material settings THEN the system uses roughness 0.8 which makes all colors appear dark gray
-
-1.7 WHEN the frontend receives utilization > 100% THEN the system displays the impossible percentage without error indication
-
-### Expected Behavior (Correct)
-
-2.1 WHEN the packing engine calculates space utilization THEN the system SHALL report utilization between 70-90% (physically possible range)
-
-2.2 WHEN cargo is placed in the container THEN the system SHALL perform 3D AABB collision detection and reject overlapping placements
-
-2.3 WHEN the backend sends packing results to the frontend THEN the system SHALL use flattened structure with direct fields (x, y, z, l, h, w, color, type) in `loadedCargo` array
-
-2.4 WHEN the frontend renders cargo boxes in 3D THEN the system SHALL display vibrant colors matching each cargo's assigned color
-
-2.5 WHEN the frontend reads color data from cargo objects THEN the system SHALL read `cargo.color` field directly from the flattened structure
-
-2.6 WHEN the 3D renderer applies material settings THEN the system SHALL use roughness 0.5 and add strong DirectionalLight for vibrant color display
-
-2.7 WHEN the frontend receives utilization > 100% THEN the system SHALL display "计算异常" error message instead of the impossible percentage
-
-### Unchanged Behavior (Regression Prevention)
-
-3.1 WHEN cargo has valid dimensions and the container has sufficient space THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO calculate correct 3D positions (x, y, z)
-
-3.2 WHEN multiple cargo items are packed successfully THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO return all cargo items in the `loadedCargo` array
-
-3.3 WHEN the packing algorithm runs with valid inputs THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO respect LIFO (Last In First Out) unloading order
-
-3.4 WHEN the 3D visualization initializes THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO create the Three.js scene with proper camera and controls
-
-3.5 WHEN cargo types are specified (appliances, furniture, etc.) THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO preserve cargo type information in the response
-
-3.6 WHEN the first cargo is placed THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO force Y=0 (ground level) placement
-
-3.7 WHEN the packing engine uses gridStep parameter THEN the system SHALL CONTINUE TO use 50mm grid resolution for stability
